From 831786ce2ba69fd391a16832959b3deff31f818d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:33:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] 0294 dsv41: TF_DS_ROUND_MS_FIT (off by default) the round
 table re-fit at the live shape

round_ms_fit is the trace's per-layer model evaluated at rows 1..24 (layer_fit.txt, fx1L,
ranks pooled, 40 target layers: 34.656 ms at 6 rows + 3.1536 ms a row), shipped behind its
own switch; the default table is unchanged and TF_DS_ROUND_MS still wins when set. The
refit script and its residual evidence are committed (tools/round_fit.py,
tools/round_fit_residuals.txt): fx1L and fx1Lb agree to 0.15%, the served table sits a
near-constant 17-19 ms over the forward (its wall share), and the live walls (todo.md:714)
imply 25.5 ms of non-forward share at 8 streams and 8.2 ms at 4 - a stream-count term a
rows-only table cannot carry (depth.zig Rule.overhead), recorded as the open decision.
