+#    8   40.96    59.1    -18.14
+#    9   44.12    62.7    -18.58
+#   10   47.27    66.3    -19.03
+#   11   50.42    69.6    -19.18
+#   12   53.58    72.9    -19.32
+#   13   56.73    75.5    -18.77
+#   14   59.89    78.2    -18.31
+#   15   63.04    81.3    -18.26
+#   16   66.19    84.4    -18.21
+#   17   69.35    87.5    -18.15
+#   18   72.50    90.6    -18.10
+#   19   75.65    93.7    -18.05
+#   20   78.81    96.8    -17.99
+#   21   81.96    99.9    -17.94
+#   22   85.11   103.0    -17.89
+#   23   88.27   106.1    -17.83
+#   24   91.42   109.2    -17.78
+# the served table sits 17.4 ms over the forward at 6 rows and 17.8 over at 24 (a near-constant wall/forward gap; its own slope 3.1 vs the trace's 3.15 ms/row)
+# wall 91.7 ms at 16 rows / 8 streams (todo.md:714 (the live eight-stream round)): wall - fitted = +25.5 ms (the non-forward share), wall - served = +7.3 ms
+# wall 87.0 ms at 20 rows / 4 streams (todo.md:714 (the measured four-stream round, ~87)): wall - fitted = +8.2 ms (the non-forward share), wall - served = -9.8 ms
+# the two walls imply 25.5 and 8.2 ms of non-forward share at 8 and 4 streams: the stream-count term a rows-only table cannot carry (depth.zig Rule.overhead). The shipped table is the forward (draft.zig's contract: a round's forward ms by its rows).
diff --git a/zig/src/families/dsv41/draft.zig b/zig/src/families/dsv41/draft.zig
index b9e4d08..3557d74 100644
